pe citations with the pinned v0.6.0 headings of the same sections. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on branch task-board/story/<STORY-ID> forked from the current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if git fetch origin shows that origin/main moved past the workspace base before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-kp4zpu and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate source, test, harness and documentation paths (no task-board.config.json, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plant files; run Python harnesses with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract: every AC sentence and every gate/refusal is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test or declared a stated bound, reported as a ratio (n of m rows driven, call site named); negatives that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; at least one NARROWING mutant per gate (a token-preserving one where a gate inspects text) executed by a shipped harness on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, subprocess return-code exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; crash/idempotency evidence with real process termination where the operation mutates durable state; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to its owner/test; LOGBOOK.md and internal TRACEABILITY.md updated without unsupported claims; no CLI or unsupported capability advertised. Authority: pinned relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6 (internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json, embedded internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md) — the section numbers in the task scope refer to the retained headings of that revision; keep historical v0.5.0 (28bf96d) behavior compatible. Reuse the landed shared owners instead of duplicating them: internal/sessrepo (repository, event chain, lease and checkpoint record attestation), internal/sessstate (state reducer), internal/sessquery (selector, plans, winning-lease admission, sealed checkpoint admission), internal/canonicaljson (closed shapes), internal/localstore (paths, projection), internal/provhost (provider identity, manifest, probe, spawn, quiesce), internal/catalog and internal/traceability (contract census; run go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck and the cataloggen -check command from task-board.config.json). Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local, never hosted; run the affected packages while iterating and the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime constructs the Change Request with a 26-command suite after your handoff — hand off no later than 3 hours in; if the scope is not finished by then, hand off a coherent partial with the ratio stated honestly rather than exceeding the budget. Attach TASK-260830-kp4zpu_results.md, TASK-260830-kp4zpu_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-kp4zpu --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: codex gpt-5.6-luna max (operator fallback while Muse Spark transport is failing). The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.","final_result":true}}}
