{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d1","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":67,"recorded_at":1780531400000129,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbbfd087327bd9edab933d31228","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer.md`.\n1|Own TASK-260830-kp4zpu (implement-provider-identity-validation), first leaf of STORY-260830-315721 (provider-identity-profile-and-resume; siblings 3uzfyn profile resolution/persistence and 2zvo8m native resume smoke framework follow you). Implement Provider Identity Record 1.0.0 creation and validation as production code: exact native session IDs, store roots, backend realms, build tuples and discovery evidence per the pinned sections 2.4, 5.5, 7.5-7.7 and 8 (provider/platform matrix), producing records that internal/provhost CheckIdentity/DecodeIdentifyResult and the landed session record/event consumers already accept — extend internal/provhost (or a sibling package it adopts) rather than duplicating its decoders, and drive the landed conformance harness from TASK-260830-32jeti; cover every refusal the sections name (wrong provider id, realm/store-root mismatch, build tuple drift, missing or unsupported discovery evidence, platform rows that are unknown/unsupported per Appendix B gates — never invent parity for a gated cell), with idempotent identity creation and no unsupported capability advertised. Replace the task's v0.5.0 scope citations with the pinned v0.6.0 headings of the same sections. Managed Story worktree contract: the Story worktree is provisioned by task-board under .temp/<STORY-ID>/worktree on branch task-board/story/<STORY-ID> forked from the current trunk; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED for the handoff snapshot, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; if git fetch origin shows that origin/main moved past the workspace base before your handoff, run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-kp4zpu and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate source, test, harness and documentation paths (no task-board.config.json, no __pycache__/.pyc, no stray plant files; run Python harnesses with PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract: every AC sentence and every gate/refusal is driven through the production entry point by a named committed test or declared a stated bound, reported as a ratio (n of m rows driven, call site named); negatives that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; at least one NARROWING mutant per gate (a token-preserving one where a gate inspects text) executed by a shipped harness on the exact final source with per-plant raw logs, subprocess return-code exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control, and NOT_APPLIED / COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE reported outside the numerator; crash/idempotency evidence with real process termination where the operation mutates durable state; a conformance matrix mapping each pinned clause to its owner/test; LOGBOOK.md and internal TRACEABILITY.md updated without unsupported claims; no CLI or unsupported capability advertised. Authority: pinned relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0 commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6 (internal/specpin/v0.6.0.lock.json, embedded internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md) — the section numbers in the task scope refer to the retained headings of that revision; keep historical v0.5.0 (28bf96d) behavior compatible. Reuse the landed shared owners instead of duplicating them: internal/sessrepo (repository, event chain, lease and checkpoint record attestation), internal/sessstate (state reducer), internal/sessquery (selector, plans, winning-lease admission, sealed checkpoint admission), internal/canonicaljson (closed shapes), internal/localstore (paths, projection), internal/provhost (provider identity, manifest, probe, spawn, quiesce), internal/catalog and internal/traceability (contract census; run go run ./internal/traceability/cmd/tracecheck and the cataloggen -check command from task-board.config.json). Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local, never hosted; run the affected packages while iterating and the full configured validation suite once before the handoff. Budget: the run has 4 hours and the runtime constructs the Change Request with a 26-command suite after your handoff — hand off no later than 3 hours in; if the scope is not finished by then, hand off a coherent partial with the ratio stated honestly rather than exceeding the budget. Attach TASK-260830-kp4zpu_results.md, TASK-260830-kp4zpu_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-kp4zpu --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: codex gpt-5.6-luna max (operator fallback while Muse Spark transport is failing). The independent reviewer will be codex gpt-6-astra low.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":68,"recorded_at":1780531400000131,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbbfe06775998c38b63fe59c03a","text":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/TASK-260830-kp4zpu_reviewer-cr1.md`.\n1|Independently review Change Request revision 1 of TASK-260830-kp4zpu (implement-provider-identity-validation, first leaf of STORY-260830-315721 provider-identity-profile-and-resume; siblings 3uzfyn profile resolution/persistence and 2zvo8m native resume smoke framework follow; task_delta on the Story branch forked from trunk 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e (tip 62d446304391af187c417a88a2e14012b467956e), published by RUN-260917-ba0926 on muse-spark max, 13 changed paths, patch and validation log attached as TASK-260830-kp4zpu_change-request_rev1.patch / _rev1-validation.log). Read the producer brief TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer.md, the outcome TASK-260830-kp4zpu_results.md, TASK-260830-kp4zpu_conformance-matrix.md, TASK-260830-kp4zpu_producer-evidence.tar.gz (gotest-*.log, mutants.json, per-plant raw logs), internal/provhost/TRACEABILITY.md in the candidate, the CR patch and validation log, and the exact immutable CR bytes. The normative authority is the pinned internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md (sections 2.4, 5.5, 7.5-7.7, 8, Appendix B); the task's own scope text still cites v0.5.0 numbering — judge against the pinned v0.6.0 headings and say so where they differ.\n2|\n3|Verify with your own instruments, never the producer's alone: (1) Spec fidelity — for each of CreateIdentity (Section 5.5 Provider Identity Record 1.0.0: member set, order, the omit-self record_id through the landed CalculateObjectIdentity owner), DecodeNativeDiscovery (Section 7.5 NativeDiscoveryProof type row), StoreRootFor (Section 8.2 table: exactly the six documented roots, Muse XDG-aware, Antigravity backend-only, Qwen and unknown refused), CheckResumeTuple (Section 8.4 native-resume direction, the Muse macOS-arm64 exact-0.1.0 pin, Appendix B gates) and VerifyIdentityBuild/VerifyIdentityDiscovery (build tuple, store root, backend realm, discovery proof binding): extract the pinned table/type rows yourself from SPEC.v0.6.0.md and diff them cell by cell against the production tables and the derivation tests (resumeProviders, discoveryMembers) — a derivation that reads a test literal instead of the pinned document is a finding; confirm no Appendix-B-gated (unknown/unsupported) cell is admitted as supported and that a passing CheckResumeTuple never advertises usable; confirm the records CreateIdentity emits are accepted by the landed CheckIdentity/DecodeIdentifyResult through Host.Call and by the session record/event consumers, and are byte-identical across repeated calls and permuted input map order. (2) Refusal census — enumerate every refusal arm of the five new entries (the producer claims 50 new arms, 217/217 witnessed, floor 166 -> 217): for each arm name the test that reaches it through the production entry with the exact code/detail; then attack the witness instrument: swap the conditions of two adjacent arms that share a code, swallow one arm into its sibling with a one-token edit, and delete one arm outright — the suite must go RED for each and you report which test caught it; report n-of-m with call sites. (3) Own plants — wrong provider id spelled with a case change; realm/store-root that differs only by a trailing slash or symlinked path; build tuple with the same version string but a different arch; discovery evidence with an extra unknown member, a missing member, a member with the right name but wrong JSON type; a Muse 0.1.0-adjacent version (0.1.0-rc1, 0.1.1, 0.10.0); an opaque id with a swapped `/` suffix; record each as admitted/refused with the code observed. (4) Mutation — rerun testdata/mutate_identity.py in an isolated copy, rerun every KILLED twice for determinism, plant at least four narrowing mutants of your own on arms the producer did not mutate (store-root compare by prefix, realm compare case-insensitive, discovery member count >= n-1, build tuple compare on version only) plus an applied harmless SURVIVED control, per-plant raw logs and subprocess exits, precise denominators (NOT_APPLIED and COMPILE_FAIL rows are unmeasured, not passes). (5) Bounds — the retained bound that no VerifyObjectIdentity call site exists outside internal/sessrepo (census the whole module); the reverseDNSPattern shared-grammar ledger row in internal/environ/census_test.go is a true one-language registration, not a diverging copy (compare the two regexes token by token and probe a string accepted by one and not the other); Section 2.4 profile authority is sibling-owned and not partially implemented here; the tenth AC row (crash evidence) is a legitimate stated bound only if every new entry is pure — grep for any file/state write. (6) Docs and hygiene — README operation-layer sentence and LOGBOOK entry make no capability/parity claim; changed_paths are exactly the 13 candidate paths, no __pycache__/.pyc, no task-board.config.json, no stray plants; tracecheck and cataloggen -check exit 0 on the exact tree; go test ./internal/provhost ./internal/environ -count=1 and -race green; go vet clean.\n4|\n5|Method: isolated immutable probes only, never mutate the live Story worktree, index, branch or HEAD; no product edits, commits, checkpoints or integration; Curator go-testing-tools skill; all CI local; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness; keep scratch small under .temp/TASK-260830-kp4zpu/ and delete candidate copies when done. Attach TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-verdict-rev1.md and TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), complete the live merged checklist, then accept_cr(TASK-260830-kp4zpu, revision=1, evidence=TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-verdict-rev1.md) or hand off changes requested with P1/P2/P3 classes named. Model: muse-spark xhigh (codex reviewers are out of quota until 2026-09-19). Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c3d5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":69,"recorded_at":1780531400000133,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"tool.result","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"tool_result","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"call_id":"call_01a0adbbfef27247987f2fdb956858a8","text":"<read-skill-result name=\"project-management\" status=\"ok\">\n<metadata>\npath: /Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/SKILL.md\nlocator: file:///Users/iv/.agents/skills/project-management/SKILL.md\nsource: user\nbytes_returned: 11930\nbytes_total: 11930\ntruncated: false\n</metadata>\n\n<skill-body id=\"project-management\">\n---\nname: project-management\ndescription: &gt;\n  File-backed task boards and spawn-first multi-agent orchestration through\n  task-board. Use for board/spec decomposition, task tracking, planning,\n  status/progress, tracked producer/reviewer runs, and delivery goals. A normal\n  primary session is the Orchestrator; a prompt-assigned role or\n  TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID is a specialist worker. Russian triggers: борд, доска,\n  задачи, эпик, стори, таски, спавн, оркестратор, субагент, статус, прогресс.\ntriggers:\n  - task board, epic, story, task, bug, status, progress\n  - spec decomposition, planning, critical path\n  - spawn, orchestrator, coordinator, sub-agent, delivery goal\n  - борд, доска, задачи, эпик, стори, таски, спавн, оркестратор\n---\n\n# Project Management Router\n\nLoad only the focused references needed. Use `task-board` for reads/writes;\nnever edit `.task-board/` directly.\n\n## Active Role\n\n- **Specialist:** when assigned a role, `TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID` exists, or the\n  human explicitly requests inline execution. Follow lifecycle/evidence gates.\n- **Orchestrator:** otherwise. Detail settled specs inline; route\n  every artifact-producing or validating task through a tracked\n  background child run. `solution-architect` only for genuine\n  architecture decisions.\n\n## Critical Invariants\n\n1. Preflight with `project_config(view=spawn-preflight, role=ROLE, agent=RUNTIME?)`;\n   bare `project_config()` stays the role-optional config surface.\n   Cross-provider ranking requires the agent-less query: omit `agent`, compare\n   recommendations, then narrow with `agent=RUNTIME` for the fresh spawn snapshot.\n   `providers.targeted` names the query&apos;s runtime scope; policy-allowed entries\n   outside it use `runtime_not_targeted_by_query`, while policy-excluded entries\n   use `provider_not_allowed_by_preferred_agentic_system`.\n   When workload recommendations are configured: query with `task_class` or an\n   explicit `workload_class`, reason about scope/risk/autonomy/validation and\n   context cost, then spawn an explicit pair with the exact class transport,\n   fresh snapshot digest, and one-line recommendation rationale. A ranking is\n   advice, never authority, a default, or permission to widen the pair.\n   For a proprietary (paid) model, choose the pair that maximises delivered\n   work per token and escalate only for a stated reason.\n   Every child has explicit role, background mode, and a complete\n   model/reasoning-effort pair across its applicable dimensions — model\n   either typed or seeded by a configured per-role default, and, for Codex,\n   Qwen, or a Claude model whose registry row declares a reasoning-effort\n   vocabulary, an in-policy effort either typed or default-seeded the same\n   way. Built-in runtimes: `agy`, `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `muse`, `qwen`\n   (plus any runtime declared under `spawn.runtimes`); Gemini, Agy,\n   `muse-spark-1.2-contributor`, and an effortless Claude model take no\n   `--reasoning-effort` at all, while `muse-spark-1.3-contributor` and its\n   `muse-spark` alias REQUIRE one from `high`/`xhigh`/`max`. The\n   versioned-short `muse-spark-1.3` names no registered row and is not\n   spawnable; codex `gpt-6-astra`/`astra` REQUIRE one of `low`/`medium`/`high`/`xhigh`/`max`/`ultra`.\n   Treat the v3 `admitted_pairs` set the\n   preflight reports as the exact admission authority, not `allowed_models`,\n   which is one input form and is `null` when the runtime uses combinable\n   `entries`; when preflight reports a v2 migration warning, use the\n   full read-only migration snapshot for an explicit reviewed repository edit.\n   Never infer admission from `PolicyRank` or silently migrate config.\n   Codex-only `fast_mode` defaults false and forces direct/managed\n   `service_tier` default/priority; preflight records root/remote provenance.\n   Remote-v4 parity is owned by the client projection and its checked fixtures;\n   authority schema v1 intentionally authorizes an empty per-board backend\n   policy set, so do not infer or add a server policy route.\n2. Workers use compact, task-specific projections. Skip routine\n   `summary()`, `plan()`, `schema()`, and `{ full }`; scoped schema only\n   repairs an unknown call.\n3. Default to `task-board spawn observe RUN --until terminal --format compact`,\n   then route its handoff. Other reads are for barriers, replay/follow,\n   diagnosis.\n4. The Orchestrator owns producer -&gt; reviewer -&gt; rework -&gt; reviewer until the\n   configured review policy is satisfied and the board reaches `done`.\n   `to-review` is a routing trigger, not human acceptance. Commit\n   decomposition is that same Orchestrator&apos;s own call, never a per-commit\n   human checkpoint.\n5. Handoff needs a task-scoped outcome and `task-board handoff TASK-ID --role\n   ROLE`. Early exits and intermediate parked states are\n   retried, or rerouted through a focused child; routine work is never handed to the human.\n   Producer `set_status(to-review)`\n   is refused, and reviewer `accept_cr` requires its live merged checklist.\n   Attach artifacts through resource CRUD under\n   `.task-board/.resources/&lt;ELEMENT-ID&gt;/`, optionally in safe nested paths;\n   never write that tree directly or attach directories.\n6. `blocked` needs an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved\n   human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist\n   constraint, evidence, failed assumptions/attempts, viable alternatives,\n   tradeoffs, recommendation, and the exact decision or external input needed.\n7. At `to-review` say **ready for review** / **handed off to review**;\n   done/complete/final only for `done`.\n8. `board-goal-v2` is authoritative: `goal` owns `parent/primary`; `spawn goal`\n   owns `run/RUN-*`. V1 shapes are compatibility-only.\n9. `openai-board` / `anthropic-board` launch the primary `task-board\n   codex|claude` sessions.\n   agents-infra composes; `tb-sessiond` owns goal bind, location-scoped\n   `openai-board|anthropic-board resume [SES-*]`, native identity restart, and\n   session operations. Provider-native adoption remains explicit as\n   `codex resume THREAD_ID` (compatibility form) or `codex --resume THREAD_ID`,\n   and `claude --resume UUID`.\n   Bad records move to private `&lt;state&gt;/quarantine/`; listen continues and\n   status/list report them.\n10. Freeze stable project/config/runtime/control roots and one binding+digest.\n    Explicit config must exist; direct/managed children override ambient roots.\n    `TASK_BOARD_DIR` stores, not authority. Resolve authority from a\n    binding via fresh `git ls-remote --symref &lt;authorized-url&gt; HEAD`,\n    exact-ref fetch, and equal advertised/fetched OIDs. Never use cached/local\n    refs, tracking, caller/config fields, or prior tuples. Cross-check\n    `integration_base_branch` against the independent branch/remote\n    pair. Zero/multiple/unavailable/indeterminate evidence refuses.\n    Producer publishes a Change Request, reviewer runs `accept_cr`,\n    then Orchestrator checkpoints leaves and integrates the Story. Managed\n    commits use `-S` with repository human identity/key; index failures never\n    justify broad reset. See\n    [tracked background spawn](references/tracked-background-spawn.md#story-worktree-isolation).\n11. Cross-Story `set_parent` and integration are durable and fail closed; move\n    evidence never widens source-tombstone admission. See\n    [tracked background spawn](references/tracked-background-spawn.md#what-the-board-state-commit-covers-and-what-it-leaves-alone).\n12. Board validation stays strict by default. The project setting\n    `validation.allow_legacy_empty_done_containers=true` suppresses only the\n    historical empty-`done` Story/Epic aggregate mismatch; active or\n    child-backed containers remain strict.\n13. Transaction-owned `.activity/&lt;ID&gt;/events.ndjson` forbids caller logging.\n    Reads are bounded; corrections privileged/append-only. Transfer/worktrees\n    reject foreign history, preserve legacy/deletion boundaries, and never backfill.\n    See [file format](references/file-formats.md#activity-streams),\n    [query](references/querying.md), and\n    [coverage](docs/activity-mutation-coverage.md).\n14. Never run `make install*`, `scripts/setup.sh`, or `task-board self-update`\n    from inside a manager-hosted session. A Claude host&apos;s PTY master lives in\n    the `tb-sessiond` process, so replacing that daemon hangs up every hosted\n    session including the caller&apos;s own. A binary swap is a human action taken\n    between sessions; the manager restarts from an outside shell with\n    `task-board session restart`. See\n    [goals recovery](references/goals-recovery.md#1-a-skill-reinstall-beside-a-running-tb-sessiond).\n\n## Decision Tree\n\n```text\nPrompt-assigned role or TASK_BOARD_RUN_ID? -&gt; work as that specialist\nArtifact, test, docs, research, or review? -&gt; tracked role-based spawn\nProducer reached to-review? -&gt; spawn reviewer, route verdict\nConcrete stop boundary? -&gt; persist packet, then blocked\nKnown structured board operation? -&gt; q/m DSL with narrow projection\nUnknown name/field? -&gt; schema(); known call syntax? -&gt; schema(operation|mutation=NAME); see querying recovery examples\n```\n\n## Lazy Reference Routes\n\n| Need | Read |\n| --- | --- |\n| Queries, observability, goals, estimates, deps | [querying](references/querying.md), [file formats](references/file-formats.md) |\n| Status, review, recovery, Stop-The-Line | [statuses](references/statuses.md) |\n| Resources, bugs, evidence | [resources and bugs](references/resources-and-bugs.md) |\n| Detailing, plans, execution | [planning workflow](references/planning-workflow.md) |\n| Research and synthesis | [research workflow](references/research-workflow.md) |\n| Roles, task classes, DoD | [roles](references/roles.md) |\n| Negative tests, gate proofs, unknown vs absence | [negative evidence](references/negative-evidence.md) |\n| Spawned goals, selection, runs, recovery, Story worktrees | [tracked background spawn](references/tracked-background-spawn.md) |\n| Change Request order, checkpoint, republish | [CR lifecycle](references/change-request-lifecycle.md) |\n| Session Manager wrappers, goal runtimes | [codex goal runtime](docs/codex-goal-runtime.md), [claude goal runtime](docs/claude-goal-runtime.md) |\n| Templates, reviewer routing | [sub-agent templates](references/sub-agent-templates.md) |\n| Context budgets | [context efficiency](references/context-efficiency.md) |\n| Config feature gates | [config features](references/config-features.md) |\n| Goal daemon skew, native recovery | [goals recovery](references/goals-recovery.md) |\n| Project config refusals/schema/examples, authority envelopes, guarded alias migration, spawn supervision in minutes | [canonical config reference](references/task-board-config.md); persist a matching scoped selection before removing legacy `remote.user`, preview with `task-board migrate-project-config`, then apply only with its reviewed `--expected-digest` |\n| Install/bootstrap | [setup](references/setup.md) |\n| Remote auth/admin/ops | [remote board runbook](docs/remote-board-operations.md) |\n| CLI/deploy overview | [README](README.md) |\n\nRuntime changes follow canonical `.specs/` contracts.\n\nBuilt-in spawn runtimes: `agy`, `claude`, `codex`, `gemini`, `muse`, `qwen`\n(plus any runtime declared under `spawn.runtimes`). Gemini CLI 0.54.4 is\ndeprecated in favour of Antigravity, but both remain supported.\n\n```bash\ntask-board spawn TASK-ID --role developer --background --agent agy --model gemini-3.6-flash-high --timeout 35m\n```\n\n`agy` takes no `--reasoning-effort`; effort is encoded in its eight scoped\nmodel IDs. Minimum `agy` is 1.1.12; 1.1.14 is validated. Prompt delivery has\na 96 KiB argv budget; `SUCCESS`/`ERROR` JSON overrides process exit. Only the\ntop-level worker is tracked. See [README](README.md) for the full models,\nflags, JSON, safety, configuration, and Gemini compatibility contract.\n\n</skill-body>\n</read-skill-result>","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_skill","outcome":"success"}}}
