{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c531","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":243,"recorded_at":1780531400000481,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adbc-4faf-7ce1-8134-36bb30908efc"},"task_id":"01a0adbc-4faf-7ce1-8134-36bb30908efc","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adbc-4faf-7ce1-8134-36bb30908efc","chunk":"Read text file `internal/provhost/identity_bind.go`.\n1|package provhost\n2|\n3|import (\n4|\t\"encoding/json\"\n5|\t\"path/filepath\"\n6|\t\"strings\"\n7|\n8|\t\"github.com/relux-works/agent-session-manager/internal/scalar\"\n9|)\n10|\n11|// This file binds Provider Identity Records to the exact native facts\n12|// they claim: the probed build tuple, the documented store root, the\n13|// backend realm, and the discovery proof a materialize or resume\n14|// observation returned. Creation (identity_create.go) builds records;\n15|// this file refuses to USE one whose facts drifted.\n16|//\n17|// The Section 8 matrices are evidence labels, not availability\n18|// promises: every gate here refuses the fail-closed direction —\n19|// unknown providers and platforms, rows the matrix marks unsupported\n20|// or unknown, and version cells the matrix pins to an exact probe —\n21|// and passing a gate never advertises a capability as usable. A row\n22|// the matrix marks conditional still requires probe acceptance at the\n23|// use site through RequireCapability; only the probe plane in Section\n24|// 7.4 establishes usable. No gate invents parity for a gated cell.\n25|//\n26|// All binding refusals are invalid_config caller errors: the caller\n27|// correlated the wrong identity, proof, or tuple. Only the discovery\n28|// proof decoder reads plugin bytes, so only its shape arms are\n29|// provider_protocol_errors with member attribution.\n30|\n31|// resumeProviders is the six Section 8.2 direct providers in table\n32|// order: the only providers with a documented native-store row. Qwen\n33|// has no direct claim and future plugins start disabled, so neither\n34|// appears here: both refuse at their own arms below, never by table\n35|// default.\n36|var resumeProviders = []string{\n37|\t\"codex\",\n38|\t\"claude\",\n39|\t\"gemini\",\n40|\t\"muse\",\n41|\t\"antigravity\",\n42|\t\"pi\",\n43|}\n44|\n45|// BuildTuple is the exact probed provider build an identity is bound\n46|// to: the Section 7.4 probe members provider_id, provider_version,\n47|// platform, and architecture. Every binding compares exact equality;\n48|// there is no normalization, no prefix match, and no version-range\n49|// evaluation, because Section 5.5 declares the range opaque adapter\n50|// data rather than a decidable grammar.\n51|type BuildTuple struct {\n52|\tProviderID      string\n53|\tProviderVersion string\n54|\tPlatform        string\n55|\tArchitecture    string\n56|}\n57|\n58|// NativeDiscovery is one validated Section 7.5 NativeDiscoveryProof:\n59|// the native session ID the proof resolved, whether discovery\n60|// succeeded, the absolute root it resolved under (present exactly\n61|// when the proof carries a non-null discovery_root), and whether the\n62|// backend resolved the ID.\n63|type NativeDiscovery struct {\n64|\tNativeSessionID  string\n65|\tDiscovered       bool\n66|\tDiscoveryRoot    string\n67|\tHasDiscoveryRoot bool\n68|\tBackendResolved  bool\n69|}\n70|\n71|// DiscoveryContext carries the host-side facts one discovery proof is\n72|// bound against: the exact probed build tuple, the home and XDG data\n73|// home the Section 8.2 store root resolves from, the expected backend\n74|// realm digest (empty when no realm is required), and the Pi session\n75|// directory override (empty for the documented default).\n76|type DiscoveryContext struct {\n77|\tBuild             BuildTuple\n78|\tHome              string\n79|\tXDGDataHome       string\n80|\tRealm             string\n81|\tStoreRootOverride string\n82|}\n83|\n84|// discoveryMembers is the exact required member set of a\n85|// NativeDiscoveryProof.\n86|var discoveryMembers = map[string]bool{\n87|\t\"native_session_id\": true,\n88|\t\"discovered\":        true,\n89|\t\"discovery_root\":    true,\n90|\t\"backend_resolved\":  true,\n91|}\n92|\n93|// discoveryRequired lists discoveryMembers in a fixed order so a proof\n94|// missing several members always names the same one.\n95|var discoveryRequired = []string{\n96|\t\"native_session_id\",\n97|\t\"discovered\",\n98|\t\"discovery_root\",\n99|\t\"backend_resolved\",\n100|}\n101|\n102|// DecodeNativeDiscovery validates one Section 7.5 NativeDiscoveryProof\n103|// body on the named platform: the exact native session ID string, the\n104|// discovered and backend_resolved booleans, and an absolute\n105|// destination-native discovery root or null. Shape violations are\n106|// provider_protocol_errors; a platform outside the registry is an\n107|// invalid_config caller error, because the proof carries no platform\n108|// and the caller named it.\n109|func DecodeNativeDiscovery(body []byte, platform string) (NativeDiscovery, error) {\n110|\tempty := NativeDiscovery{}\n111|\tif !isProbePlatform(platform) {\n112|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"discovery platform is not a registry member\")\n113|\t\tif err != nil {\n114|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n115|\t\t}\n116|\t\treturn empty, failure\n117|\t}\n118|\tmembers, fault := decodeStrictObject(body)\n119|\tif fault != nil {\n120|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(fault.detail, fault.member)\n121|\t\tif err != nil {\n122|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n123|\t\t}\n124|\t\treturn empty, failure\n125|\t}\n126|\tif name, unknown := unknownMember(members, discoveryMembers); unknown {\n127|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery carries unknown member\", name)\n128|\t\tif err != nil {\n129|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n130|\t\t}\n131|\t\treturn empty, failure\n132|\t}\n133|\tif name, missing := missingMember(members, discoveryRequired); missing {\n134|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery misses a required member\", name)\n135|\t\tif err != nil {\n136|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n137|\t\t}\n138|\t\treturn empty, failure\n139|\t}\n140|\tnative, ok := rawString(members[\"native_session_id\"])\n141|\tif !ok || runeLength(native) < 1 || runeLength(native) > 512 {\n142|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery native_session_id is not 1..512 characters\", \"native_session_id\")\n143|\t\tif err != nil {\n144|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n145|\t\t}\n146|\t\treturn empty, failure\n147|\t}\n148|\tdiscovered, ok := rawBool(members[\"discovered\"])\n149|\tif !ok {\n150|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery discovered is not a boolean\", \"discovered\")\n151|\t\tif err != nil {\n152|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n153|\t\t}\n154|\t\treturn empty, failure\n155|\t}\n156|\troot, isNull, ok := rawNullableString(members[\"discovery_root\"])\n157|\tif !ok || (!isNull && !isAbsoluteOn(root, scalar.Platform(platform))) {\n158|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery discovery_root is not an absolute path or null\", \"discovery_root\")\n159|\t\tif err != nil {\n160|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n161|\t\t}\n162|\t\treturn empty, failure\n163|\t}\n164|\tbackendResolved, ok := rawBool(members[\"backend_resolved\"])\n165|\tif !ok {\n166|\t\tfailure, err := failProtocol(\"discovery backend_resolved is not a boolean\", \"backend_resolved\")\n167|\t\tif err != nil {\n168|\t\t\treturn empty, err\n169|\t\t}\n170|\t\treturn empty, failure\n171|\t}\n172|\treturn NativeDiscovery{\n173|\t\tNativeSessionID:  native,\n174|\t\tDiscovered:       discovered,\n175|\t\tDiscoveryRoot:    root,\n176|\t\tHasDiscoveryRoot: !isNull,\n177|\t\tBackendResolved:  backendResolved,\n178|\t}, nil\n179|}\n180|\n181|// StoreRootFor resolves the Section 8.2 documented native-store root\n182|// for one provider under the given home. It returns the absolute root,\n183|// or backendOnly when the provider identifies through a backend realm\n184|// rather than a filesystem store. XDG data home applies to Muse only;\n185|// an empty value selects the documented default below ~/.local/share.\n186|// Refusals are invalid_config caller errors: Qwen has no direct claim,\n187|// unknown providers start disabled, and a non-absolute home cannot\n188|// anchor a store.\n189|func StoreRootFor(providerID, home, xdgDataHome string) (string, bool, error) {\n190|\tif !validProviderID(providerID) {\n191|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store provider is not a provider id\")\n192|\t\tif err != nil {\n193|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n194|\t\t}\n195|\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n196|\t}\n197|\tif home == \"\" {\n198|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store home is empty\")\n199|\t\tif err != nil {\n200|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n201|\t\t}\n202|\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n203|\t}\n204|\tif !isBareAbsolute(home) {\n205|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store home is not an absolute path\")\n206|\t\tif err != nil {\n207|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n208|\t\t}\n209|\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n210|\t}\n211|\tif providerID == \"qwen\" {\n212|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store has no direct qwen claim\")\n213|\t\tif err != nil {\n214|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n215|\t\t}\n216|\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n217|\t}\n218|\tif !isResumeProvider(providerID) {\n219|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store names an unknown provider\")\n220|\t\tif err != nil {\n221|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n222|\t\t}\n223|\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n224|\t}\n225|\t// Antigravity identifies through the destination-authenticated\n226|\t// backend realm, not a filesystem store: Section 8.2 names no\n227|\t// durable root, and Appendix B leaves the SQLite root unsettled.\n228|\tif providerID == \"antigravity\" {\n229|\t\treturn \"\", true, nil\n230|\t}\n231|\tif providerID == \"muse\" && xdgDataHome != \"\" {\n232|\t\tif !isBareAbsolute(xdgDataHome) {\n233|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"store xdg data home is not an absolute path\")\n234|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n235|\t\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n236|\t\t\t}\n237|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n238|\t\t}\n239|\t\treturn filepath.Join(xdgDataHome, \"muse\", \"sessions\"), false, nil\n240|\t}\n241|\tif providerID == \"codex\" {\n242|\t\treturn filepath.Join(home, \".codex\", \"sessions\"), false, nil\n243|\t}\n244|\tif providerID == \"claude\" {\n245|\t\treturn filepath.Join(home, \".claude\", \"projects\"), false, nil\n246|\t}\n247|\tif providerID == \"gemini\" {\n248|\t\treturn filepath.Join(home, \".gemini\"), false, nil\n249|\t}\n250|\tif providerID == \"muse\" {\n251|\t\treturn filepath.Join(home, \".local\", \"share\", \"muse\", \"sessions\"), false, nil\n252|\t}\n253|\t// Only pi reaches here: six-membership is proven above and every\n254|\t// other member returned. A seventh table member must extend this\n255|\t// chain in the same change; the pairwise-distinctness test below\n256|\t// the chain fails a provider silently aliased onto pi's root.\n257|\treturn filepath.Join(home, \".pi\", \"agent\", \"sessions\"), false, nil\n258|}\n259|\n260|// CheckResumeTuple enforces the Section 8.4 native-resume direction\n261|// for one exact probed build tuple: unknown providers and platforms\n262|// refuse, the Qwen direct row refuses, the Muse native-Windows unknown\n263|// cell refuses, and a Muse macOS arm64 build refuses unless it is the\n264|// exact 0.1.0 probe the cell accepts, because Appendix B leaves every\n265|// newer Muse behavior unsettled with enabled false. Available and\n266|// conditional rows pass this gate; passing never advertises usable,\n267|// and conditional rows still require probe acceptance at the use site.\n268|func CheckResumeTuple(tuple BuildTuple) error {\n269|\tif !validProviderID(tuple.ProviderID) {\n270|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume provider is not a provider id\")\n271|\t\tif err != nil {\n272|\t\t\treturn err\n273|\t\t}\n274|\t\treturn failure\n275|\t}\n276|\tif runeLength(tuple.ProviderVersion) < 1 || runeLength(tuple.ProviderVersion) > 128 {\n277|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume version is not 1..128 characters\")\n278|\t\tif err != nil {\n279|\t\t\treturn err\n280|\t\t}\n281|\t\treturn failure\n282|\t}\n283|\tif !isProbePlatform(tuple.Platform) {\n284|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume platform is not a registry member\")\n285|\t\tif err != nil {\n286|\t\t\treturn err\n287|\t\t}\n288|\t\treturn failure\n289|\t}\n290|\tif !isProbeArchitecture(tuple.Architecture) {\n291|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume architecture is not amd64 or arm64\")\n292|\t\tif err != nil {\n293|\t\t\treturn err\n294|\t\t}\n295|\t\treturn failure\n296|\t}\n297|\tif tuple.ProviderID == \"qwen\" {\n298|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume has no direct qwen claim\")\n299|\t\tif err != nil {\n300|\t\t\treturn err\n301|\t\t}\n302|\t\treturn failure\n303|\t}\n304|\tif !isResumeProvider(tuple.ProviderID) {\n305|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume names an unknown provider\")\n306|\t\tif err != nil {\n307|\t\t\treturn err\n308|\t\t}\n309|\t\treturn failure\n310|\t}\n311|\tif tuple.ProviderID == \"muse\" && tuple.Platform == \"windows\" {\n312|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume is unknown on this tuple\")\n313|\t\tif err != nil {\n314|\t\t\treturn err\n315|\t\t}\n316|\t\treturn failure\n317|\t}\n318|\tif tuple.ProviderID == \"muse\" && tuple.Platform == \"macos\" && tuple.Architecture == \"arm64\" && tuple.ProviderVersion != \"0.1.0\" {\n319|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"resume is unverified for this muse version\")\n320|\t\tif err != nil {\n321|\t\t\treturn err\n322|\t\t}\n323|\t\treturn failure\n324|\t}\n325|\treturn nil\n326|}\n327|\n328|// VerifyIdentityBuild binds one Provider Identity Record to the exact\n329|// probed build tuple: the tuple must pass the Section 8.4 resume\n330|// gate, the record must validate for the tuple's provider, and the\n331|// record's exact probed version must equal the tuple's version. Any\n332|// drift between the identity's build facts and the probed facts\n333|// refuses, because a mapping or resume decision made for one build\n334|// must never silently apply to another.\n335|func VerifyIdentityBuild(identityBody []byte, tuple BuildTuple) error {\n336|\tif err := CheckResumeTuple(tuple); err != nil {\n337|\t\treturn err\n338|\t}\n339|\tif err := CheckIdentity(identityBody, tuple.ProviderID); err != nil {\n340|\t\treturn err\n341|\t}\n342|\t// The members below replay the record CheckIdentity just proved\n343|\t// well-formed, never the raw body: the fault is nil by\n344|\t// construction, following the RequireCapability pattern, so no\n345|\t// refusal can drift between the validation and the use.\n346|\tmembers, _ := decodeStrictObject(identityBody)\n347|\tversion, _ := rawString(members[\"provider_version\"])\n348|\tif version != tuple.ProviderVersion {\n349|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"build version drifted from the probed tuple\")\n350|\t\tif err != nil {\n351|\t\t\treturn err\n352|\t\t}\n353|\t\treturn failure\n354|\t}\n355|\treturn nil\n356|}\n357|\n358|// VerifyIdentityDiscovery binds one Provider Identity Record to one\n359|// discovery proof under the host's discovery context: the identity\n360|// must bind to the probed build tuple, the proof must decode on the\n361|// tuple's platform, its exact native ID must equal the identity's, it\n362|// must report discovery, its root must sit at or under the Section 8.2\n363|// store root (or the Pi override), and its backend resolution must\n364|// cover the identity's realm claim and the expected realm. A null\n365|// proof root is refused for filesystem providers; backend providers\n366|// carry no root rule because no documented root exists to bind.\n367|func VerifyIdentityDiscovery(identityBody, proofBody []byte, ctx DiscoveryContext) error {\n368|\tif err := VerifyIdentityBuild(identityBody, ctx.Build); err != nil {\n369|\t\treturn err\n370|\t}\n371|\tproof, err := DecodeNativeDiscovery(proofBody, ctx.Build.Platform)\n372|\tif err != nil {\n373|\t\treturn err\n374|\t}\n375|\tmembers, _ := decodeStrictObject(identityBody)\n376|\tnative, _ := rawString(members[\"native_session_id\"])\n377|\tif proof.NativeSessionID != native {\n378|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind native id does not equal the identity\")\n379|\t\tif err != nil {\n380|\t\t\treturn err\n381|\t\t}\n382|\t\treturn failure\n383|\t}\n384|\tif !proof.Discovered {\n385|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind discovery evidence is absent\")\n386|\t\tif err != nil {\n387|\t\t\treturn err\n388|\t\t}\n389|\t\treturn failure\n390|\t}\n391|\tif err := checkBindStoreRoot(proof, ctx); err != nil {\n392|\t\treturn err\n393|\t}\n394|\tif err := checkBindRealm(proof, members, ctx.Realm); err != nil {\n395|\t\treturn err\n396|\t}\n397|\treturn nil\n398|}\n399|\n400|// checkBindStoreRoot requires the proof root at or under the expected\n401|// store root: the Pi override when the caller sets one, else the\n402|// Section 8.2 documented root. Backend providers return before any\n403|// root rule, because identity there resolves through the realm.\n404|func checkBindStoreRoot(proof NativeDiscovery, ctx DiscoveryContext) error {\n405|\texpected, backendOnly, err := resolveBindRoot(ctx)\n406|\tif err != nil {\n407|\t\treturn err\n408|\t}\n409|\tif backendOnly {\n410|\t\treturn nil\n411|\t}\n412|\tif !proof.HasDiscoveryRoot {\n413|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind discovery root is missing\")\n414|\t\tif err != nil {\n415|\t\t\treturn err\n416|\t\t}\n417|\t\treturn failure\n418|\t}\n419|\tif !rootContains(expected, proof.DiscoveryRoot) {\n420|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind discovery root is outside the provider store\")\n421|\t\tif err != nil {\n422|\t\t\treturn err\n423|\t\t}\n424|\t\treturn failure\n425|\t}\n426|\treturn nil\n427|}\n428|\n429|// resolveBindRoot selects the expected store root: the caller override\n430|// for Pi, whose Section 8.2 row documents\n431|// PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR and --session-dir, else the Section 8.2\n432|// documented root. Any other provider's override refuses: the surface\n433|// is documented for Pi only, and no provider inherits it by default.\n434|func resolveBindRoot(ctx DiscoveryContext) (string, bool, error) {\n435|\tif ctx.StoreRootOverride != \"\" {\n436|\t\tif ctx.Build.ProviderID != \"pi\" {\n437|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind store override is pi-only\")\n438|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n439|\t\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n440|\t\t\t}\n441|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n442|\t\t}\n443|\t\tif !isAbsoluteOn(ctx.StoreRootOverride, scalar.Platform(ctx.Build.Platform)) {\n444|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind store override is not an absolute path\")\n445|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n446|\t\t\t\treturn \"\", false, err\n447|\t\t\t}\n448|\t\t\treturn \"\", false, failure\n449|\t\t}\n450|\t\treturn ctx.StoreRootOverride, false, nil\n451|\t}\n452|\treturn StoreRootFor(ctx.Build.ProviderID, ctx.Home, ctx.XDGDataHome)\n453|}\n454|\n455|// checkBindRealm requires the proof's backend resolution to cover the\n456|// identity's realm claim and the caller's expected realm: an expected\n457|// realm must be a digest the identity carries exactly, and a\n458|// non-null identity realm requires backend_resolved, because the\n459|// realm is a resume precondition wherever it is set.\n460|func checkBindRealm(proof NativeDiscovery, members map[string]json.RawMessage, wantRealm string) error {\n461|\trealm, isNull, _ := rawNullableString(members[\"backend_realm_fingerprint\"])\n462|\tif wantRealm != \"\" {\n463|\t\tif !isDigest(wantRealm) {\n464|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind expected realm is not a digest\")\n465|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n466|\t\t\t\treturn err\n467|\t\t\t}\n468|\t\t\treturn failure\n469|\t\t}\n470|\t\tif isNull || realm != wantRealm {\n471|\t\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind realm does not equal the expected backend realm\")\n472|\t\t\tif err != nil {\n473|\t\t\t\treturn err\n474|\t\t\t}\n475|\t\t\treturn failure\n476|\t\t}\n477|\t}\n478|\tif !isNull && !proof.BackendResolved {\n479|\t\tfailure, err := failInvalid(\"bind backend realm is claimed but unresolved\")\n480|\t\tif err != nil {\n481|\t\t\treturn err\n482|\t\t}\n483|\t\treturn failure\n484|\t}\n485|\treturn nil\n486|}\n487|\n488|// isResumeProvider reports whether the provider carries a Section 8.2\n489|// direct native-store row. It ranges resumeProviders, never a sample:\n490|// a validation that held for three providers and skipped the rest\n491|// would pass a tuple this gate must refuse.\n492|func isResumeProvider(providerID string) bool {\n493|\tfor _, provider := range resumeProviders {\n494|\t\tif providerID == provider {\n495|\t\t\treturn true\n496|\t\t}\n497|\t}\n498|\treturn false\n499|}\n500|\n(more lines below)","final_result":true}}}
