{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c629","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":367,"recorded_at":1780531400000729,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0adbc-8967-7ff2-9721-d5022767962b"},"task_id":"01a0adbc-8967-7ff2-9721-d5022767962b","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0adbc-8967-7ff2-9721-d5022767962b","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-7-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"8\\\\.2\\\\|Native-store\\\\|native-store\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 20; echo ===; grep -n \\\"codex/sessions\\\\|claude/projects\\\\|gemini/tmp\\\\|muse/sessions\\\\|pi/agent\\\" internal/specdoc/SPEC.v0.6.0.md | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Locate Section 8.2 store rows in spec\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"102:[the Muse and Antigravity evidence report](.research/260819_muse-antigravity-native-store-contracts.md),\\n523:    sockets, and absolute native-store paths are not mesh directory records.\\n743:enrichment worker as session, workspace, native-store, or lease authority.\\n860:every workspace, provider native-store, task-board staging, credential,\\n2000:| <code>provider_manifest_id</code> | digest or null | Direct native-store/provider snapshot only |\\n2831:    \\\"native-store-plan\\\",\\n3143:| <code>native-store-plan</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanRequest</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, identity:Provider Identity Record, source_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_platform:macos&#124;linux&#124;wsl2&#124;windows, destination_host_id:UUIDv7, mode:snapshot&#124;handoff&#124;fork, source_manifest_id:digest, destination_workspace_paths:WorkspacePaths, lease:LeaseToken}</code> | Tagged <code>NativeStorePlanResult</code>: capture is <code>{phase:capture, capture_plan:ProviderCapturePlan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128]}</code>; materialize is <code>{phase:materialize, materialization_plan:Materialization Plan, include_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], exclude_classes:sorted unique string[0..128], path_key_rewrites:map(UUIDv7,string[1..1024])[0..256]}</code> |\\n3167:calls <code>native-store-plan phase=materialize</code> with\\n3176:secret environment values. <code>native-store-plan</code> succeeds only for an\\n3190:destination-local native-store root for the exact adapter tuple, and be\\n3308:uses no unlisted native-store root. A composite plan is therefore one host\\n3927:### 8.2 Native-store contract matrix\\n3995:| Qwen task-board prompt mode / any target platform | U direct; A only where task-board probe reports <code>prompt_spawn</code> | No direct native-store or primary-owner claim. |\\n5544:token. Provider <code>native-store-plan</code> returns this schema with optional\\n6396:#### 10.8.2 Conversation Lineage and annotations\\n7009:  Section 10.8.2. When the representative is unmanaged,\\n7910:output, PIDs/PTYs/sockets, absolute native-store paths, runtime observations,\\n9029:   <code>native-store-plan phase=capture</code> and <code>capture</code> with the\\n9155:IDs replacing PID/native-store reconciliation:\\n9397:- no local process is using the proposed destination native-store/workspace\\n===\\n3246:        \\\"root_path\\\": \\\"/Users/iv/.codex/sessions\\\",\\n3931:| Codex | Session UUID/name; known root <code>~/.codex/sessions</code>. Source absolute cwd is metadata. | <code>codex resume SESSION_ID</code>; current CLI also has <code>codex fork SESSION_ID</code>. | Adapter MUST stage only the closed session objects it has identified, compute the destination cwd mapping, validate discovery by explicit ID, and merge without replacing unrelated sessions. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until cross-host fixtures pass. | Authentication files, config secrets, MCP tokens, logs not required by the session, live processes, locks, SQLite/WAL/SHM, and runtime sockets. |\\n3932:| Claude | Session UUID; known root <code>~/.claude/projects</code> with a provider-computed project key. | <code>claude --resume SESSION_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, and <code>--fork-session</code> when resuming. | Adapter MUST derive the destination project key from the logical workspace mapping, stage the closed session plus documented companion data, and validate explicit UUID resume. It MUST NOT copy the source project-directory key verbatim as identity. <code>portable_store</code> remains C. | OAuth/API credentials, settings secrets, MCP auth, live PTY state, PID/lock/socket files, caches, and unproven companion databases. |\\n3933:| Gemini CLI | Session UUID scoped by logical project; documented root <code>~/.gemini/tmp/&lt;project-hash&gt;/chats</code>. | <code>gemini --resume UUID</code>, picker/index/latest, and <code>--session-file FILE</code>. | Adapter MUST compute the destination project hash, prefer the documented session-file import when compatible, stage atomically, then validate <code>--list-sessions</code> and explicit UUID resume. <code>portable_store</code> is C until schema/version and cross-platform fixtures pass. | Google credentials, API keys, settings secrets, trust state, runtime locks, cache-only files, and source path keys. |\\n3934:| Muse | Session UUID; <code>$XDG_DATA_HOME/muse/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/UUID</code>, defaulting below <code>~/.local/share</code>. | <code>muse resume UUID</code>, <code>--last</code>, picker, and <code>muse exec --session-id UUID</code>. Export exists; native import does not. | On probed macOS 0.1.0, a guarded adapter MAY stage the complete closed durable directory, omit transient files, validate with offline export, and resume explicitly. It MUST advertise <code>portable_store = false</code> because cron-aware, current-version, cross-host fidelity is not proven. | <code>~/.config/muse/auth.json</code>, keys, login state, <code>.session.lock</code>, sockets/tokens, live WAL/SHM/locks, updater/plugin caches. <code>cron.db</code> is durable but not safely portable; a session with active or non-empty scheduled work MUST fail materialization. |\\n3936:| Pi | Session UUID/file; <code>~/.pi/agent/sessions</code> or the configured <code>PI_CODING_AGENT_SESSION_DIR</code>/<code>--session-dir</code>. | <code>--session PATH_OR_ID</code>, <code>--continue</code>, <code>--resume</code>, <code>--fork</code>. | Adapter MUST snapshot a closed JSONL session and required non-secret companion data, map the destination cwd/session directory, validate the session ID, and resume explicitly. <code>portable_store</code> remains C until versioned cross-host fixtures pass. | <code>auth.json</code>, provider keys/tokens, extension secrets, live process state, locks, sockets, and caches. Pi 0.73.1 has no YOLO flag. |\\n5432:      \\\"root_path\\\": \\\"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\\\",\\n5643:  \\\"authorities\\\": [{\\\"authority_id\\\":\\\"codex_sessions\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"provider_store\\\",\\\"platform\\\":\\\"linux\\\",\\\"root_path\\\":\\\"/home/ivan/.codex/sessions\\\",\\\"provider_id\\\":\\\"codex\\\",\\\"root_role\\\":\\\"durable_store\\\",\\\"write_policy\\\":\\\"managed_merge\\\"}],\\n5692:    \\\"schema\\\":\\\"urn:ax:schema:materialization-plan\\\",\\\"schema_version\\\":\\\"1.0.0\\\",\\\"plan_id\\\":\\\"sha256:158f1dedc6711daacee7b9b6d777aea201d2e8cf9df351593f2ada793e8908e5\\\",\\\"kind\\\":\\\"workspace\\\",\\\"intent\\\":\\\"passive_replica\\