{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d1ef","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0adbb-d982-7d33-a597-bf4c4953f6b8"},"sequence":1874,"recorded_at":1780531400003743,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"run_terminal","command_id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5d52738d-e67a-4909-b1e5-6f3604d03379"},"terminal":"completed","text":"Accepted — `CR-TASK-260830-kp4zpu-1` rev 1 is now `accepted`, task routing to `integrating`. No findings; live tree left untouched (HEAD still `62d4463`, only the 13 candidate paths present, no commits).\n\nWhat I verified with my own instruments (all in isolated copies; raw logs in `TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`):\n\n- **Spec fidelity**: re-extracted the §8.2 rows and §7.5 `NativeDiscoveryProof` row from `SPEC.v0.6.0.md` — byte-identical to the embedded v0.5.0 rows the derivation tests pin, so the v0.5.0-vs-v0.6.0 numbering gap is immaterial. `resumeProviders` 6/6, `discoveryMembers` 4/4, six store roots cell-by-cell, Muse macOS-arm64 exact-`0.1.0` pin, no gated cell admitted. Round-trip through `Host.Call` and byte-identical idempotency both pass.\n- **Refusal census**: 50/50 new arms driven with exact code/detail; 217/217 derived arms witnessed. Three witness attacks (swap adjacent conditions, one-token `==`→`!=` swallow, delete qwen arm) all went RED via named tests.\n- **Own plants**: 15 probes — case-change provider refused ×3, trailing-slash root refused fail-closed, symlink root refused, codex arch change admitted (no pin; version equality is the rule), discovery extra/missing/wrong-type refused, Muse `0.1.0` admitted with `rc1`/`0.1.1`/`0.10.0` refused, trailing-slash opaque admitted per the absolute-prefix wording.\n- **Mutation**: producer harness rerun twice — 24/24 KILLED both runs, identical classifications; plus 4/4 of my own narrowing mutants on unmutated arms killed and a harmless control survived.\n- **Bounds/gates**: `VerifyObjectIdentity` only in `sessrepo`; `reverseDNSPattern` is one language (`()` vs `(?:)` only); zero profile refs in new files; new entries make no durable writes, so the crash-evidence stated bound holds. Pkg tests, `-race`, `vet`, `tracecheck`, `cataloggen -check`, `gofmt` all exit 0.\n\nOne non-blocking note (in the verdict): Gemini resolves the `~/.gemini` base rather than the full per-project-hash root — disclosed by the producer, and inventing the hash would be worse. Verdict and evidence attached as `TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-verdict-rev1.md` and `TASK-260830-kp4zpu_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`; checklist 19/19; scratch copies deleted.","reason":null}}
